> Time: 1438101280 / Tue, 28 Jul 2015 16:34:40 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic/getPosts?topicId=79025&start=10&SessionId=2685917f70402f51eb74a5aaab2b38f7
> User jacquewedding (283943)
Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"190.241.252.27","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79025,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5c6da877f0b80bd974f22d2287850b84","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Moments that Matter, Our travel planner told us that Arenal is not showing lava these days and has not been for a couple of years :( I ad read about that and saw photos but I do not think it is going to happen. I would LOVE to see lava though, that would be new for me!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;ACW71011, I have never been to Jamaica. We like to travel and have done the obligatory Bahamas trip, we went to Antigua once and both are lovely. We love Cancun and Mexico. I will NEVER forget the beaches at Tulum south of Cancun. Swimming in the water with Mayan ruins all around is surreal. I always wanted to see Jamaica, I love Reggae music and would love to visit the birth place of it.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;How exciting you are going to Costa Rica next year too! I will definately report back on the trip! You can try our girl Catalina, I can&#039;s say enough about her. As I understand she has a small company and is the owner. We researched her and a few others, it was a toss up in the end but I feel we made the right choice. ccuervo@crreferrals.com&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I want to jump forward a month NOW! :P Time to poke around some more.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Thank you for being so welcoming and your kind responses!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1892187,"PostDate":1428418314,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Moments that Matter, Our travel planner told us that Arenal is not showing lava these days and has not been for a couple of years <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> I ad read about that and saw photos but I do not think it is going to happen. I would LOVE to see lava though, that would be new for me!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>ACW71011, I have never been to Jamaica. We like to travel and have done the obligatory Bahamas trip, we went to Antigua once and both are lovely. We love Cancun and Mexico. I will NEVER forget the beaches at Tulum south of Cancun. Swimming in the water with Mayan ruins all around is surreal. I always wanted to see Jamaica, I love Reggae music and would love to visit the birth place of it.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>How exciting you are going to Costa Rica next year too! I will definately report back on the trip! You can try our girl Catalina, I can's say enough about her. As I understand she has a small company and is the owner. We researched her and a few others, it was a toss up in the end but I feel we made the right choice. ccuervo@crreferrals.com<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I want to jump forward a month NOW! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/> Time to poke around some more.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thank you for being so welcoming and your kind responses!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cassidymichaels233@gmail.com","IpAddress":"190.241.252.27","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1428321137,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"youngandinlove","Id":282649,"Name":"youngandinlove","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.137.211.49","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79025,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"109506a758a8fea49b87b022c319af9a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congrats!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1892442,"PostDate":1428536234,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congrats!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"phimoez@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"50.137.211.49","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1425862236,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"MNsunseeker","Id":282367,"Name":"MNsunseeker","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79025,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"708b391f862035b914a343d49405e857","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congrats!&amp;nbsp; Your date is coming up really fast.&amp;nbsp; My instructor just went came from Costa rica and she fell in love.&amp;nbsp; She said it was by far her top travel place.&amp;nbsp; It&#039;s very safe and beautiful.&amp;nbsp; The beaches are obviously not going to be as stunning as Tulum but everything is like super amazing!!!&amp;nbsp; :)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1892480,"PostDate":1428577336,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congrats!\u00a0 Your date is coming up really fast.\u00a0 My instructor just went came from Costa rica and she fell in love.\u00a0 She said it was by far her top travel place.\u00a0 It's very safe and beautiful.\u00a0 The beaches are obviously not going to be as stunning as Tulum but everything is like super amazing!!!\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Married on June 20th, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess Riviera Gazebo & Reception at the Chill Out with 60 guests<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>My review thread: \u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79344-grand-sunset-princess-platinum-yucatan-princess-wedding\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1396968452,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1435850174","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"190.241.252.17","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79025,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1437412549,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0d93f57301ca8fb2d9b46b1622ea76c2","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hola!!! (see? I can speak some spanish now!&amp;nbsp;\n\n\nI wanted to write a quick follow up. My BIG day has come and gone. We were married (eloped) on Flamingo Beach in Costa Rica. Everything went perfectly.\n\n\nOur wedding planner was Catalina Cuervo from C.R. Referrals Travel. (&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.costaricavacationexperts.com&#039;&gt;www.costaricavacationexperts.com&lt;\/a&gt;). They are located in Costa Rica and Catalina is the owner. She personally plans each wedding herself from what I was told. Catalina did an amazing job lining up the photographer, the officiate, and even arranged a candlelight chefs table on the beach. We had a private waiter and the head chef attending us, it was like it was from a storybook. We wanted something romantic but simple. We wanted to spend our money more on an amazing trip, not just all on the ceremony and Catalina made it all possible. From the moment we landed, we were taken very good care of. If you ever get to read this Catalina, Thank You! (I already sent her like 4 messages thanking her)\n\n\nI found this Destination Wedding website late in my planning but I did get some valuable advice in my reading. We ended up having to fiddle with the dates a little but it all worked out. Thanks to the encouragement of others, I did bring my mothers wedding dress and was married in it. She is no longer with us and this was so important to me. Thank you for your comments regarding the dress in another post I had done, it made it there and back again in one piece. I like to dream of my own daughter maybe using the same dress someday. 3 generations married in my family with the same dress would be wonderful. First, I need to have a daughter, we are working on that   :wub:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here is what we did on our elope\/adventure\n\n\nMay ~15th ~ Day 1 ~ Arrival ~ Liberia airport\n\n\u2022 Private Transfer to Playa Flamingo - this took about a little over 2 hours to get to the resort\n\n\u2022 Flamingo beach Resort \u2013 Honeymoon Suite - Right on the beach, we loved the attention to service they had.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~16th ~ Day 2 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ (B,L,D)\n\n\u2022 Catamaran &amp;amp; Snorkeling Tour - A lovely catamaran tour. We had hoped to see whales but did not, we did see dolphins and huge Manta Rays jumping out of the water! The sunset was beautiful and it was a nice introduction.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~17th ~ Day 3 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ (B,L,Private dinner on the beach)\n\n\u2022 Wedding Day!!!!!!!!\n\n\u2022 2:00pm Couples Massage - who does not like a massage?&amp;nbsp;\n\n\u2022 3:30pm Hair &amp;amp; Makeup - This was handled by the resort and coordinated with our wedding planner Catalina\n\n\u2022 4:30pm Photographer - We had some pre ceremony photos, during and after\n\n\u2022 5:20pm wedding on the beach \u2013 ceremony - We had some touch and go moments on the weather, but in the end we got the beach wedding we wanted&amp;nbsp;\n\n\u2022 legal wedding officiate - arranged by Catalina\n\n\u2022 6:15 Wedding Dinner \u2013 private chef\u2019s table on the beach - This was magical, this was an 8 course tasting menu prepared by the head chef. He personally delivered each course along with our private waiter. I felt like royalty at this point in the day.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~18th ~ Day 4 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ (B,L,D)\n\n\u2022 Buena Vista Combo Tour - This was an adventure day. The tour included several fun activities including horseback riding, canopy tours, hanging bridges, volcanic mud baths, it was heavenly&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~19th ~ Day 5 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ Arenal ~ (&amp;nbsp;\n\n\u2022 Private transfer to Arenal - this was a long transfer, about 5 hours almost with a stop we made for lunch and at a road side fruit stand.\n\n\u2022 Check in Silencio del Campo \u2013 cabin\/villa - Loved, loved, loved this small hotel. It has hot springs that are heated from Arenal Volcano, wonderful volcano views, it was just lovely and so nice to soak in the hot springs each night.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~20th ~ Day 6 ~ Arenal ~ (&amp;nbsp;\n\n\u2022 Safari Float - A nice river float, we saw monkeys, sloths, many birds, it was a nice relaxed day.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~21st ~ Day 7 ~ Arenal ~ (B,L)\n\n\u2022 Canyoneering &amp;amp; River Rafting - This was our final day of adventure. It included rappelling down waterfalls in the rainforest and then rafting down rapids in a river! It was an intense day but SO much fun. Both my HUSBAND (love saying that word now) and I are nature lovers, and adventure seekers. This was the perfect ending to our Adventure\/Elopement\/Honeymoon&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;May ~22nd ~ Day 8 ~ Departure ~ (&amp;nbsp; ~ Liberia\n\n\u2022 Private Transfer to Airport - The trip back to the airport took about 3 hours.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I am waiting on the final photos from the photographer, that is probably the only negative. We have the preliminary photos, they look good but I want to post the final touched up pics when we get them. It should be soon, there is a 3 month turn around on touched up final photos.\n\n\nTo anyone wanting to get married or elope in another country, do it! The entire trip cost us about $6000 with airfare. We calculated getting married back at home, after the venue and wedding plans it would have cost us a fortune, the way we did it we had a wonderful celebration of our love and had money left over&amp;nbsp;\n\n\nThank you for your time in answering my questions and bless everyone who enters into marriage, I hope your lives together are special beyond words. If I can help anyone with any questions I would be more than happy.\n\n\nXXOO,\n\n\nCassidy&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900802,"PostDate":1437412245,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hola!!! (see? I can speak some spanish now!\u00a0<br><br>\nI wanted to write a quick follow up. My BIG day has come and gone. We were married (eloped) on Flamingo Beach in Costa Rica. Everything went perfectly.<br><br>\nOur wedding planner was Catalina Cuervo from C.R. Referrals Travel. (<a href='http:\/\/www.costaricavacationexperts.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>www.costaricavacationexperts.com<\/a>). They are located in Costa Rica and Catalina is the owner. She personally plans each wedding herself from what I was told. Catalina did an amazing job lining up the photographer, the officiate, and even arranged a candlelight chefs table on the beach. We had a private waiter and the head chef attending us, it was like it was from a storybook. We wanted something romantic but simple. We wanted to spend our money more on an amazing trip, not just all on the ceremony and Catalina made it all possible. From the moment we landed, we were taken very good care of. If you ever get to read this Catalina, Thank You! (I already sent her like 4 messages thanking her)<br><br>\nI found this Destination Wedding website late in my planning but I did get some valuable advice in my reading. We ended up having to fiddle with the dates a little but it all worked out. Thanks to the encouragement of others, I did bring my mothers wedding dress and was married in it. She is no longer with us and this was so important to me. Thank you for your comments regarding the dress in another post I had done, it made it there and back again in one piece. I like to dream of my own daughter maybe using the same dress someday. 3 generations married in my family with the same dress would be wonderful. First, I need to have a daughter, we are working on that\u00a0\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wub.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':wub:' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Here is what we did on our elope\/adventure<br><br>\nMay ~15th ~ Day 1 ~ Arrival ~ Liberia airport<br>\n\u2022 Private Transfer to Playa Flamingo - this took about a little over 2 hours to get to the resort<br>\n\u2022 Flamingo beach Resort \u2013 Honeymoon Suite - Right on the beach, we loved the attention to service they had.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~16th ~ Day 2 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ (B,L,D)<br>\n\u2022 Catamaran & Snorkeling Tour - A lovely catamaran tour. We had hoped to see whales but did not, we did see dolphins and huge Manta Rays jumping out of the water! The sunset was beautiful and it was a nice introduction.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~17th ~ Day 3 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ (B,L,Private dinner on the beach)<br>\n\u2022 Wedding Day!!!!!!!!<br>\n\u2022 2:00pm Couples Massage - who does not like a massage?\u00a0<br>\n\u2022 3:30pm Hair & Makeup - This was handled by the resort and coordinated with our wedding planner Catalina<br>\n\u2022 4:30pm Photographer - We had some pre ceremony photos, during and after<br>\n\u2022 5:20pm wedding on the beach \u2013 ceremony - We had some touch and go moments on the weather, but in the end we got the beach wedding we wanted\u00a0<br>\n\u2022 legal wedding officiate - arranged by Catalina<br>\n\u2022 6:15 Wedding Dinner \u2013 private chef\u2019s table on the beach - This was magical, this was an 8 course tasting menu prepared by the head chef. He personally delivered each course along with our private waiter. I felt like royalty at this point in the day.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~18th ~ Day 4 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ (B,L,D)<br>\n\u2022 Buena Vista Combo Tour - This was an adventure day. The tour included several fun activities including horseback riding, canopy tours, hanging bridges, volcanic mud baths, it was heavenly\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~19th ~ Day 5 ~ Playa Flamingo ~ Arenal ~ (\u00a0<br>\n\u2022 Private transfer to Arenal - this was a long transfer, about 5 hours almost with a stop we made for lunch and at a road side fruit stand.<br>\n\u2022 Check in Silencio del Campo \u2013 cabin\/villa - Loved, loved, loved this small hotel. It has hot springs that are heated from Arenal Volcano, wonderful volcano views, it was just lovely and so nice to soak in the hot springs each night.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~20th ~ Day 6 ~ Arenal ~ (\u00a0<br>\n\u2022 Safari Float - A nice river float, we saw monkeys, sloths, many birds, it was a nice relaxed day.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~21st ~ Day 7 ~ Arenal ~ (B,L)<br>\n\u2022 Canyoneering & River Rafting - This was our final day of adventure. It included rappelling down waterfalls in the rainforest and then rafting down rapids in a river! It was an intense day but SO much fun. Both my HUSBAND (love saying that word now) and I are nature lovers, and adventure seekers. This was the perfect ending to our Adventure\/Elopement\/Honeymoon\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May ~22nd ~ Day 8 ~ Departure ~ (\u00a0 ~ Liberia<br>\n\u2022 Private Transfer to Airport - The trip back to the airport took about 3 hours.<\/p>\n<p>I am waiting on the final photos from the photographer, that is probably the only negative. We have the preliminary photos, they look good but I want to post the final touched up pics when we get them. It should be soon, there is a 3 month turn around on touched up final photos.<br><br>\nTo anyone wanting to get married or elope in another country, do it! The entire trip cost us about $6000 with airfare. We calculated getting married back at home, after the venue and wedding plans it would have cost us a fortune, the way we did it we had a wonderful celebration of our love and had money left over\u00a0<br><br>\nThank you for your time in answering my questions and bless everyone who enters into marriage, I hope your lives together are special beyond words. If I can help anyone with any questions I would be more than happy.<br><br>\nXXOO,<br><br>\nCassidy<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cassidymichaels233@gmail.com","IpAddress":"190.241.252.27","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1428321137,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"youngandinlove","Id":282649,"Name":"youngandinlove","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"142.161.170.48","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79025,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5defd8eda58e72abd2696d5bba25da36","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Just checking in to see how your wedding went, Cassidy? would LUV to hear all about it - if you&#039;d like to share - Congrats and enjoy your new life together going forward - Cheers!!! team MTM :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-ord1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xft1\/t31.0-8\/11722583_10153446505144487_4643870793731625409_o.jpg\" alt=\"11722583_10153446505144487_4643870793731\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1900852,"PostDate":1437483044,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Just checking in to see how your wedding went, Cassidy? would LUV to hear all about it - if you'd like to share - Congrats and enjoy your new life together going forward - Cheers!!! team MTM <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-ord1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xft1\/t31.0-8\/11722583_10153446505144487_4643870793731625409_o.jpg\" alt=\"11722583_10153446505144487_4643870793731\"><\/span><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><img src=\"http:\/\/i711.photobucket.com\/albums\/ww116\/momentsthatmatter\/MTMLogo08-1.png\" alt=\"MTMLogo08-1.png\"><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.momentsthatmatterphotography.com'><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Moments That Matter Photography Studios, Playa del Carmen, Mexico<\/span><\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Canadian Award Winning Photojournalist serving Mayan Riviera<br>\nEmail: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com'>contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Scoop on what we do:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/r\/4212-beautiful-november-wedding\/#review'>MTM Reviews<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Meet Lincoln & Team MTM: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/vimeo.com\/51032621'>\"Meet Lincoln\" Video + see his Passion!!!<\/a>","Email":"momentsthatmatterphotography@gmail.com","IpAddress":"189.221.252.187","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1280196260,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230711.png?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Moments That Matter","Id":230711,"Name":"Moments That Matter","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":15,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
